#!/bin/bash
# ABOUTME: Instant pass.
#
# This is an instructor-led workshop. A real check would have to inspect the
# attendee's own edits, and the only way to make one pass on demand is a solve
# script that writes over their work - which is worse than no check at all.
#
# An instant pass is the right trade whenever the failure mode is loud. Here it
# is louder than anywhere else in the track: this challenge has nothing to
# edit, so the only thing a check could gate on is whether someone watched a
# script print numbers. Gating that pushes a stuck learner into Skip, and Skip
# runs the solve script over their terminal for no benefit at all.
exit 0
